  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Three capacitors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> are connected as shown in the figure. Find the ratio of the charges on capacitors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> respectively.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c1cf4765-f469-494f-ba88-c60aebcb7f82-image.png\" style=\"width: 246px; height: 178px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "210F0",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SegoG",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oAl40",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
